  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 1795 K, melting point of Er; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.757$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{0} = 8.421 + 0.312 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.839 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.421\\times10^{-3}T+0.156\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.839\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.806$ \nFormation equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1795 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hf}^{\\circ} = -10.146 - 0.474 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 1.355 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 121.600 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = -10.146 + 0.474 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 1.355 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 60.800 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 22.219 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n1795-2000 K: $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = -11.800 - 4.444 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.095 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 61.300 T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = -11.800 + 4.444 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.095 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 30.650 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 48.775 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Pedley (396). ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "Phase change: 1795 K, melting point of Er; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.757$ kcal/mol.",
